	"notes": "This is a Substack blog, and it never gets wider than 1280 pixels no matter the screen — on an ultrawide monitor it just floats in the middle with empty blue on both sides, so the reading experience is identical on a laptop and on a giant screen. Inside that fixed-width block, a desktop shows two columns: the list of posts on the left, and a narrow column on the right with the author's photo, a subscribe box, and lists of other things to read. On a phone that narrow column is not stacked below the feed the way most sidebars are — it just disappears, and the phone gets only the post list. The first automatic scan guessed this page was one plain centred column (`1-centered`); looking at the actual pictures shows a real two-column sidebar living inside that centred box, which is the more accurate call and the two calls disagreeing is itself worth knowing.",
